  "notes": [
    "The manager could only overwrite keepers once it owned EthCrossChainData; that ownership grant, made 64 blocks after the manager's deployment, gave the defective contract the power the exploit used and is the reset. Later writes to the data contract are keeper and epoch values the attack overwrote.",
    "Campaign: every successful manager call after each chain's keeper replacement (Ethereum, BSC, Polygon), including one Ethereum relayer transaction that delivered an attacker-signed renBTC unlock. Sibling managers on BSC and Polygon are the same template.",
    "Loss is gross LockProxy depletion; the assets the attacker returned are not subtracted. DefiLlama lacks BSC BUSD history, so BUSD is valued at the Binance USD market price."
  ]
